    {
      "id": "eYVcqscXC3_yClgn3TPET",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 641.60546875,
      "y": 6686.66796875,
      "width": 876.2394409179688,
      "height": 950,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aS",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 771397696,
      "version": 1108,
      "versionNonce": 912563136,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1766158571614,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "             |\n             |\n      Node has taint?\n             |\n             |\n      Pod tolerates?\n       |           |\n       |            |\n       No.         Yes\n       |.              |\n       |           Schedule \n      Reject     \n                   \n      handson\n       kubectl get nodes\n       kind-control-plane\n       kind-worker\n       kind-worker2\n       \ntaint -> kubectl taint nodes kind-worker dedicated=database:NoSchedule\n           kubectl describe node kind-worker | grep Taint\n normal pod: pod.yaml will not work. because it is not tolerant to schedule on worker-node\nafter adding toleration: kubectl apply -f toleration-pod.yaml\nnow it will tolerate the taint.\n\ntypes of taints:'\n3 types are there\n\n1. NoExecute(Eviction mode)\nnode unhealthy\nsecurity breath\nspot instance termination\nkubectl taint nodes kind-worker critical=true:NoExecute\nexisting pod will alse evicted.\nML Workload\ninfra pods for monitoring\nbanking workload\ngpu",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "             |\n             |\n      Node has taint?\n             |\n             |\n      Pod tolerates?\n       |           |\n       |            |\n       No.         Yes\n       |.              |\n       |           Schedule \n      Reject     \n                   \n      handson\n       kubectl get nodes\n       kind-control-plane\n       kind-worker\n       kind-worker2\n       \ntaint -> kubectl taint nodes kind-worker dedicated=database:NoSchedule\n           kubectl describe node kind-worker | grep Taint\n normal pod: pod.yaml will not work. because it is not tolerant to schedule on worker-node\nafter adding toleration: kubectl apply -f toleration-pod.yaml\nnow it will tolerate the taint.\n\ntypes of taints:'\n3 types are there\n\n1. NoExecute(Eviction mode)\nnode unhealthy\nsecurity breath\nspot instance termination\nkubectl taint nodes kind-worker critical=true:NoExecute\nexisting pod will alse evicted.\nML Workload\ninfra pods for monitoring\nbanking workload\ngpu",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ja8Kbk9kxKNrNuwbFFJB-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 643.92578125,
      "y": 7685.77734375,
      "width": 597.7595825195312,
      "height": 600,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aT",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 964402112,
      "version": 509,
      "versionNonce": 1874119616,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1766158736236,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. No Schedule\nNew pod will not schedule\nexisting pods stay running\ndb nodes\ngpu nodes\nbanking workloads\ndedicated infra nodes\n\nkubectl taint node gpu-node gpu=true:NoSchedule\n\npod.yaml\ntoleration:\n\n3. PreferNoSchedule(soft block)\n\nScheduler will try to avoid using this node\nbut it will schedule the pod on this node \nonly if other nodes are not available.\n\npartially reserved nodes.\nlegacy workloads.\ncost-saving clusters\n\nkubectl taint node worker-node2 spot=true:PreferNoSchedule",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2. No Schedule\nNew pod will not schedule\nexisting pods stay running\ndb nodes\ngpu nodes\nbanking workloads\ndedicated infra nodes\n\nkubectl taint node gpu-node gpu=true:NoSchedule\n\npod.yaml\ntoleration:\n\n3. PreferNoSchedule(soft block)\n\nScheduler will try to avoid using this node\nbut it will schedule the pod on this node \nonly if other nodes are not available.\n\npartially reserved nodes.\nlegacy workloads.\ncost-saving clusters\n\nkubectl taint node worker-node2 spot=true:PreferNoSchedule",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "uR842NMw3oDxVDG3WU0ty",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 655.74609375,
      "y": 8327.8125,
      "width": 761.99169921875,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
